@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Partner Search Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account partner search works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sea.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SEA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | sea.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | SEA                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Seapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| SEAPARSEAPAR |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| SEAKORKORSEA |
	| SEAKOR       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| SEAPARSEAPAR |
	| SEAKORKORSEA |
	| SEAKOR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Seapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Seakor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View advanced search results
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and add the project partner in koroneiki and view the project partner view advanced search results

	Given I generate past static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | SEA                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | SEA                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korsea - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | SEAPARSEAPAR                                   | |
	| Contact Email Address | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken           | |
	| Description           | Test provisioning partner account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-9012                                   | |
	| Name                  | Seapar - ${staticProjectName}                  | |
	| Profile Email Address | sea.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken           | |
	| Region                | United States                                  | |
	| Status                | Active                                         | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                             | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikipartner.com                       | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Perpetual   | true     | |
	| Quantity    | 1        | |
	| Status      | Approved | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	And I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" assigned to the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I update a koroneiki account with the name "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" including nested fields to have the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" on the account "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I expand the account advanced search form
	And I populate the advanced search form with the following values and search
	| Match              |               | Radio Button | All                              |
	| Account Name       |               | Input        | Seapar - ${staticProjectName}    |
	| Code               |               | Input        | SEAPARSEAPAR                     |
	| Account            |               | Panel        | Collapse                         |
	| Categorization     |               | Panel        | Expand                           |
	| Partner            | Yes           | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Provides FLS       | Yes           | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Receives FLS       | No            | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Internal           | No            | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Subscription State | Active        | Checkbox     | false                            |
	| Subscription State | Cancelled     | Checkbox     | false                            |
	| Subscription State | Expired       | Checkbox     | false                            |
	| Subscription State | Unactivated   | Checkbox     | false                            |
	| Tier               | T4            | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Support Region     | United States | Checkbox     | true                             |
	| Categorization     |               | Panel        | Collapse                         |
	| Dates              |               | Panel        | Expand                           |
	| Created After      |               | Input        | ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}     |
	| Created Before     |               | Input        | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate} |
	| Modified After     |               | Input        | ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}     |
	| Modified Before    |               | Input        | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate} |
	| Date               |               | Panel        | Collapse                         |
	Then I should be able to view an account on the provisioning index with the name "Seapar - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name    | Seapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code    | SEAPARSEAPAR                  |
	| Region  | United States                 |
	| Tier    | T4                            |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Code: SEAPARSEAPAR                                |
	| Label | Account Name: Seapar - ${staticProjectName}       |
	| Label | Partner: Yes                                      |
	| Label | Provides FLS: Yes                                 |
	| Label | Receives FLS: No                                  |
	| Label | Internal: No                                      |
	| Label | Tier: T4                                          |
	| Label | Support Region: United States                     |
	| Label | Modified After: ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}      |
	| Label | Modified Before: ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate} |
	| Label | Created Before: ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate}  |
	| Label | Created After: ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}       |
	When I go to the account index page
	And I expand the account advanced search form
	And I populate the advanced search form with the following values and search
	| Match               |               | Radio Button  | All                              |
	| Account Name        |               | Input         | Korsea - ${staticProjectName}    |
	| Code                |               | Input         | SEAKORKORSEA                     |
	| Partner/Reseller/SI |               | Select Entity | Seapar - ${staticProjectName}    |
	| First Line Support  |               | Select Entity | Seapar - ${staticProjectName}    |
	| Country             |               | Select        | United States                    |
	| Account             |               | Panel         | Collapse                         |
	| Categorization      |               | Panel         | Expand                           |
	| Partner             | No            | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Provides FLS        | No            | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Receives FLS        | Yes           | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Internal            | No            | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Tier                | T4            | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Subscription State  | Active        | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Subscription State  | Cancelled     | Checkbox      | false                            |
	| Subscription State  | Expired       | Checkbox      | false                            |
	| Subscription State  | Unactivated   | Checkbox      | false                            |
	| Subscription Level  | Platinum      | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Support Region      | United States | Checkbox      | true                             |
	| Categorization      |               | Panel         | Collapse                         |
	| Dates               |               | Panel         | Expand                           |
	| Created After       |               | Input         | ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}     |
	| Created Before      |               | Input         | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate} |
	| Modified After      |               | Input         | ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}     |
	| Modified Before     |               | Input         | ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate} |
	| Date                |               | Panel         | Collapse                         |
	Then I should be able to view an account on the provisioning index with the name "Korsea - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name    | Korsea - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code    | SEAKORKORSEA                  |
	| Partner | Seapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Region  | United States                 |
	| SLA     | Platinum                      |
	| Tier    | T4                            |
	| State   | ACTIVE                        |
	And I should be able to view the search info message with the following types and values
	| Label | Country: United States                             |
	| Label | Code: SEAKORKORSEA                                 |
	| Label | Account Name: Korsea - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Label | Partner/Reseller/SI: Seapar - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Label | First Line Support: Seapar - ${staticProjectName}  |
	| Label | Partner: No                                        |
	| Label | Provides FLS: No                                   |
	| Label | Receives FLS: Yes                                  |
	| Label | Internal: No                                       |
	| Label | Tier: T4                                           |
	| Label | Subscription State: Active                         |
	| Label | Subscription Level: Platinum Subscription          |
	| Label | Support Region: United States                      |
	| Label | Modified After: ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}       |
	| Label | Modified Before: ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate}  |
	| Label | Created Before: ${staticYyyyMmDdFutureStartDate}   |
	| Label | Created After: ${staticYyyyMmDdPastEndDate}        |

Scenario: View advanced search results after partner update via provisioning
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and add the project partner in the provisioning page account details and view the project partner view advanced search results

	Given I generate past static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I generate future static yyyymmdd start and end dates
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Seakor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | sea.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | SEA                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
